{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1180638-what-is-dexterity-used-for-in-combat","id":1180638,"title":"What is Dexterity used for in combat?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-30T01:17:06-08:00","id":1180638,"title":"What is Dexterity used for in combat?","content":"Close combat is explicitly governed by Might, and with ranged weapons, at the range band you can use dexterity, you can also use Might. <br /> <br /> And determining Defence defaults to Stamina...<br /> <br /> I know Dex used to be the god stat, but come on, this is a bit of an over adjustment!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 01-30-2018, 04:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T01:57:51-08:00","id":1180644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1180638-what-is-dexterity-used-for-in-combat#post1180638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Close combat is explicitly governed by Might, and with ranged weapons, at the range band you can use dexterity, you can also use Might.</div> </div> </div> </div>Incorrect. Here is a direct quote from the book &quot;In a Physical underground boxing match, a fighter could dive in and hammer away with Might (Force), weave around for a perfect shot with Dexterity (Finesse), or drain his opponent with a Stamina (Resilience) rope-a-dope.&quot;. Looks like Dex is a go for close combat if you want, and so is Stamina. Now I know what part you are referring to (pg 140/141), yet even there the table doesn't match with the proceeding paragraph. So, since there are already rules for varied approaches with combat skills, and this table doesn't even agree with the lead in... I think it's safe to ignore it as something that just hasn't hit an editor yet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1180638-what-is-dexterity-used-for-in-combat#post1180638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And determining Defense defaults to Stamina...</div> </div> </div> </div>According to Neall in the Makeshift Character Sheet thread Defense &quot;Generally it's highest Physical, but I'll mark it for clarification.&quot; once again, Dex is good to go.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1180638-what-is-dexterity-used-for-in-combat#post1180638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I know Dex used to be the god stat, but come on, this is a bit of an over adjustment!</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Every dramatic challenge in the game exists in one of three different Arenas, reflecting the abilities it requires and obstacles it involves. On every role, the <b>Storyguide determines the Arena of a challenge</b>.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;A character\u2019s Approach defines the way they tackle challenges. <b>Whenever a character faces a challenge requiring a roll, their player should describe their Approach after the Storyguide decides the Arena</b>.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>TLDR</b>: Dex is fine, all attributes are good now, players now choose what attribute they roll for any given task.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T02:20:54-08:00","id":1180650,"title":"","content":"Ah, that makes sense and sounds pretty awesome! Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T06:10:38-08:00","id":1180684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1180638-what-is-dexterity-used-for-in-combat?p=1180644#post1180644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incorrect. Here is a direct quote from the book &quot;In a Physical underground boxing match, a fighter could dive in and hammer away with Might (Force), weave around for a perfect shot with Dexterity (Finesse), or drain his opponent with a Stamina (Resilience) rope-a-dope.&quot;. Looks like Dex is a go for close combat if you want, and so is Stamina. Now I know what part you are referring to (pg 140/141), yet even there the table doesn't match with the proceeding paragraph. So, since there are already rules for varied approaches with combat skills, and this table doesn't even agree with the lead in... I think it's safe to ignore it as something that just hasn't hit an editor yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I took that example to be a physical challenge, not combat. I thought it was pretty clear on pg 133 under Attacking when it says&quot; melee attacks is Close Combat + Might&quot; and in other places where it specifically says which Attributes are used for what.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1180638-what-is-dexterity-used-for-in-combat?p=1180644#post1180644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to Neall in the Makeshift Character Sheet thread Defense &quot;Generally it's highest Physical, but I'll mark it for clarification.&quot; once again, Dex is good to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>On pg 108 under Defense it does say &quot;character's Physical Resilience Attribute&quot; but then goes on to say &quot;Stamina, Resolve, Composure&quot; and explain how calm or collected characters can avoid attacks with equal alacrity. That's the typo. It's backed up later on pg 32 under Defending, &quot;you roll the highest Resistance Attribute&quot;. (Which looks like another typo, but I think it's obvious that Resistance = Resilience.) So you can use Composure or Resolve, but not Dexterity. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1180638-what-is-dexterity-used-for-in-combat?p=1180644#post1180644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Every dramatic challenge in the game exists in one of three different Arenas, reflecting the abilities it requires and obstacles it involves. On every role, the <b>Storyguide determines the Arena of a challenge</b>.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;A character\u2019s Approach defines the way they tackle challenges. <b>Whenever a character faces a challenge requiring a roll, their player should describe their Approach after the Storyguide decides the Arena</b>.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Despite those quotes, which are great advice for general, dramatic challenges, we do have more specific rules for some things, like combat, which do call out certain dice pools for certain rolls.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> As far as the usefulness of Dexterity in combat, it's still good for Down and Dirty Combat, which makes dice pools in the more general way, ambushes and surprise attacks, and Short and Medium range attacks. It's not useful for melee combat, but Dex covers the what are probably the most used range bands outside of close. It's a good Attribute to have for most Firearms use.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T07:13:08-08:00","id":1180698,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but what about character concepts like &quot;rapier duelist that uses speed and precision over brute strength&quot; or &quot;martial artist whose style relies on a flurry of weak blows rather than a single strong blow&quot;? <br /> <br /> Like, I'm not really expecting them to change the rule in the book, because I think we're past that point, but I'm at least willing to entertain the idea of house ruling the use of dexterity for attack for certain character archetypes.<br /> <br /> Although, I suppose one way to do it is to come up with your own weapon tag.<br /> Finesse [1] - This weapon can use Dexterity instead of Might to attack in melee.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9296-zeldafan42","name":"Zeldafan42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9296_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T08:01:12-08:00","id":1180715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1180638-what-is-dexterity-used-for-in-combat?p=1180684#post1180684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I took that example to be a physical challenge, not combat. I thought it was pretty clear on pg 133 under Attacking when it says&quot; melee attacks is Close Combat + Might&quot; and in other places where it specifically says which Attributes are used for what.<br /> <br /> On pg 108 under Defense it does say &quot;character's Physical Resilience Attribute&quot; but then goes on to say &quot;Stamina, Resolve, Composure&quot; and explain how calm or collected characters can avoid attacks with equal alacrity. That's the typo. It's backed up later on pg 32 under Defending, &quot;you roll the highest Resistance Attribute&quot;. (Which looks like another typo, but I think it's obvious that Resistance = Resilience.) So you can use Composure or Resolve, but not Dexterity.<br /> <br /> Despite those quotes, which are great advice for general, dramatic challenges, we do have more specific rules for some things, like combat, which do call out certain dice pools for certain rolls.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> As far as the usefulness of Dexterity in combat, it's still good for Down and Dirty Combat, which makes dice pools in the more general way, ambushes and surprise attacks, and Short and Medium range attacks. It's not useful for melee combat, but Dex covers the what are probably the most used range bands outside of close. It's a good Attribute to have for most Firearms use.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Combat appears to be called out explicitly as something that's not always Might <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Brawling may be a test of physical force (i.e., Close Combat + Might), but it may also be a test of mental control (i.e., Close Combat + Cunning) as a character focuses on finding weaknesses to exploit. The Skills section on p. XX lists some common pairings, but those are only suggestions. </div> </div> </div>I don't see any way to read that other than using non-Might for Close Combat attacks.<br /> <br /> There's also this bit: <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Close Combat Attack<br /> You strike your opponent at close range, either with a weapon or without.<br /> Range: Close<br /> Skill: Close Combat<br /> Hit: Overcome the target\u2019s Defense<br /> Stunts </div> </div> </div> Note how, unlike Grappling, it just lists a skill and not a skill + attribute<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Range: Close<br /> Skill: Agility (Might)<br /> Hit: Overcome the opponent's Defense </div> </div> </div> At this point, I think the most sensible read is that it changed relatively recently, and there's some conflicting information that will need clarifying at some point. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T12:28:24-08:00","id":1180847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1180638-what-is-dexterity-used-for-in-combat?p=1180684#post1180684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I took that example to be a physical challenge, not combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Boxing &quot;IS&quot; combat. You both give, and receive, damage...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1180638-what-is-dexterity-used-for-in-combat?p=1180684#post1180684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought it was pretty clear on pg 133 under Attacking when it says&quot; melee attacks is Close Combat + Might&quot; and in other places where it specifically says which Attributes are used for what.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is clearly an example of the person who wrote the combat chapter not understanding the system they are writing for, and just assuming that D&amp;D'isms still held true. This game has gone under so many internal revisions that at least one of the sample characters is an illegal build, and the example character doesn't follow the rules of character creation that they are supposed to be showcasing. When combined with all the other examples of misplaced words, and other errors it becomes quite clear that this book desperately needs a new editor, and writers who know the system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1180638-what-is-dexterity-used-for-in-combat?p=1180684#post1180684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On pg 108 under Defense it does say &quot;character's Physical Resilience Attribute&quot; but then goes on to say &quot;Stamina, Resolve, Composure&quot; and explain how calm or collected characters can avoid attacks with equal alacrity. That's the typo. It's backed up later on pg 32 under Defending, &quot;you roll the highest Resistance Attribute&quot;. (Which looks like another typo, but I think it's obvious that Resistance = Resilience.) So you can use Composure or Resolve, but not Dexterity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know what it says on pg 108... However Neall, the line developer, when it was posted in the Makeshift Character Sheet Thread &quot;Defense description is sort of confusing. Went with equal to the highest of all resistance attributes&quot; he replied &quot;Generally it's highest Physical, but I'll mark it for clarification.&quot;. So apparently the PDF is wrong... who knew...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1180638-what-is-dexterity-used-for-in-combat?p=1180684#post1180684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Despite those quotes, which are great advice for general, dramatic challenges, we do have more specific rules for some things, like combat, which do call out certain dice pools for certain rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>And those rules are suspect at best. In real life Might, Dexterity, and Stamina are all useful to different styles of Close Combat fighting, and grappling in particular. My personal style of grappling is more Stamina based, I wear you down until you make a mistake, my brothers is Might based, he tries to overwhelm you from the start, and my cousin is a slippery little beast that is definitely Dexterity based. I was so enthusiastic when I read approaches because it was finally a system that allowed the flexibility of action choice that I see in real life... and then came the combat chapter...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1180638-what-is-dexterity-used-for-in-combat?p=1180684#post1180684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as the usefulness of Dexterity in combat, it's still good for Down and Dirty Combat, which makes dice pools in the more general way, ambushes and surprise attacks, and Short and Medium range attacks. It's not useful for melee combat, but Dex covers the what are probably the most used range bands outside of close. It's a good Attribute to have for most Firearms use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you ever shot a firearm, as in &quot;in real life&quot;? Not &quot;I've played video games&quot;, or &quot;watched a video on it&quot;, but actually received professional training on how to take a life? Accuracy by volume (Might), Control/Hammer Pairs (Dexterity), and One Shot, One Kill/Waiting for the shot (Stamina) are all valid tactics, depending on the situation, for Ranged Combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T13:00:21-08:00","id":1180854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1180638-what-is-dexterity-used-for-in-combat?p=1180847#post1180847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One Kill/Waiting for the shot (Stamina) are all valid tactics, depending on the situation, for Ranged Combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with the gist your going for here, and this'll probably even go to improve upon it, but i think that particular example is probably best to pair with Composure. <br /> <br /> Actually Stamina might be the only one im not sure that could actually pair with trying to shoot someone (Or atleast i can't think of a scenario). Cunning and Intellect could be used to extrapolate patterns or trick them out, same for manipulation. You could use Presence to taunt them towards rash actions and shoot them, Might and Dexterity are obvious, Resolve could be cold and focused skill, etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T13:25:00-08:00","id":1180866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1180638-what-is-dexterity-used-for-in-combat?p=1180854#post1180854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with the gist your going for here, and this'll probably even go to improve upon it, but i think that particular example is probably best to pair with Composure.<br /> <br /> Actually Stamina might be the only one im not sure that could actually pair with trying to shoot someone (Or atleast i can't think of a scenario). Cunning and Intellect could be used to extrapolate patterns or trick them out, same for manipulation. You could use Presence to taunt them towards rash actions and shoot them, Might and Dexterity are obvious, Resolve could be cold and focused skill, etc</div> </div> </div> </div>The shear physicality of waiting, in one spot, for hours, trying for that perfect shot, can not be overstated. Also, don't forget that in the Storypath System \u201cthe Storyguide determines the Arena of a challenge\u201d Physical, Mental, or Social, and the player then describes how their character approaches that task.<br /> <br /> For example, lets say you are trying to shoot someone. I, as the SG in this scenario decide that this is going to be a Physical task. You, as the player in all this, are well within your rights to describe your character \u201cpatiently waiting for just the right moment\u201d and roll Stamina to reflect that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T14:05:54-08:00","id":1180878,"title":"","content":"I was under the impression that an &quot;Arena&quot; was a narrative scenario and did not apply to combat? IE: your ST can't just declare that your using mental skills for this combat when you really just want to punch him in the mouth real good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T14:24:32-08:00","id":1180883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1180638-what-is-dexterity-used-for-in-combat?p=1180878#post1180878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was under the impression that an &quot;Arena&quot; was a narrative scenario and did not apply to combat? IE: your ST can't just declare that your using mental skills for this combat when you really just want to punch him in the mouth real good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me quote the book on Arena's &quot;Every <b><i>dramatic challenge</i></b> in the game exists in one of three different Arenas, reflecting the abilities it requires and obstacles it involves. <b>On every role, the Storyguide determines the Arena of a challenge</b>.&quot; Dramatic Challenge, not Narrative, and let me be clear. You say what you want to do. &quot;I'm going to punch him.&quot; and based on your stated desire of action, the SG determines the arena, never the player. You get your input on the Arena when you determine your attempted action, after the Arena is determined by the SG, the player then chooses his approach based upon the circumstances of the scene, and his chosen style.<br /> <br /> If you disagree with the SG, it is up to the social contract at your own individual table as to how you go about bringing up your disagreement, and working thru it, if your contract includes such things, but ultimately it is the SG's call. If you don't trust the SG to make a fair call as to the Arena, then why are you playing in their game?<br /> <br /> *Furthermore, Arenas are chosen for each action individually. Not for combat as a whole. Psy-Ops, Tactics, and Force all have their place in any given combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","user":"TheSarcasticSage","date":".  *Edit 01-30-2018, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T14:35:51-08:00","id":1180888,"title":"","content":"I'm not an expert on guns, but i think that ''controlling your breathing'' might be a nice way to tie stamina with shooting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T15:56:43-08:00","id":1180917,"title":"","content":"Looks like the rules are in conflict.<br /> <br /> And I have used a gun, thank you, albeit just target practice.<br /> <br /> I didn't bring up what concepts worked or didn't work, or what makes &quot;sense&quot;, just trying to read the rules. I usually will assume specific rules will override the general (as in this case, the general lick your Approach vs specific combat Attributes called out -- because really, why have those specific rules if they don't actually matter?)<br /> <br /> Anyway, it'd be good to get some clarification on this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}